  "goodToKnow": "Die Streitkräfte are the armed forces, always used in the plural: die russischen Streitkräfte, die US-Streitkräfte. Germany's are called die Bundeswehr, founded in 1955; East Germany had the Nationale Volksarmee. Since 2022, Germany has been investing heavily in its Streitkräfte with a special fund of 100 billion euros. Literally, the word means fighting forces: streiten (to fight, argue) + die Kraft (force)."
